Flag.description:
Boolean flag with explicit enable/disable constructors.

```rust
use solti_model::Flag;

let f = Flag::enabled();
assert!(f.is_enabled());

let f: Flag = false.into();
assert!(f.is_disabled());

let b: bool = f.into();
assert!(!b);
```

KeyValue.description:
Key-value pair used for environment variables or generic metadata.

## Example

```
use solti_model::KeyValue;

let kv = KeyValue::new("APP_MODE", "batch");
assert_eq!(kv.key(), "APP_MODE");
assert_eq!(kv.value(), "batch");
```

SubprocessMode.description:
Execution strategy for a subprocess task.

| Variant   | Fields                              |
|-----------|-------------------------------------|
| `Command` | executable and arguments            |
| `Script`  | interpreter, base64 body, arguments |

## Example

```
use base64::Engine;
use base64::engine::general_purpose::STANDARD as BASE64;
use solti_exec::subprocess::SubprocessMode;

let mode = SubprocessMode::Script {
    interpreter: "bash".into(),
    body: BASE64.encode("echo hello"),
    args: vec![],
};

assert_eq!(mode.decode_body().unwrap(), "echo hello");
```

TaskEnv.description:
Environment variables passed to a task at submission time.

Duplicate keys are allowed. Lookup uses last-value-wins semantics.

```
use solti_model::TaskEnv;

let mut env = TaskEnv::new();
env.push("APP_MODE", "dev");
env.push("APP_MODE", "prod");

assert_eq!(env.get("APP_MODE"), Some("prod"));
```
